{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788067386880226001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"random-decayable-armadillo","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"afb126be9d24566191195b8e19b2864eb50854ea7af5137f3e5e7222f794e50f","event_uuid":"fa8f48bd-0ec8-49f5-bd40-9f4fbf5f7801","position":{"commit_sha":"938bf7a51b33b60af8b3c8f275ec42399282a471","position":"1788065418785021617-fa8f48bd-0ec8-49f5-bd40-9f4fbf5f7801"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a985f1315b3bc1b559860e5833975df0b0998a97be9a06b14b89aed7c6d189d1","event_uuid":"4b5dd541-ba86-492c-9aa0-dc9d30bf1995","position":{"commit_sha":"3624eb470431d90633300b5577a9f021c344bdcc","position":"1788065440783051129-4b5dd541-ba86-492c-9aa0-dc9d30bf1995"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a00ac2067a7c0da2c207cb56079c4c30b1dd2666140f99f353674a212b96c6c0","event_uuid":"7d128dcf-627c-4789-81a2-f5afd8a0a6f4","position":{"commit_sha":"2bf3dd3f764b887a0205c975e4eb0f001fdb6b98","position":"1788065441712756929-7d128dcf-627c-4789-81a2-f5afd8a0a6f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788065418785021617,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4b5dd541-ba86-492c-9aa0-dc9d30bf1995","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b580-98b6-d9b7-4817"},{"link_uuid":"7d128dcf-627c-4789-81a2-f5afd8a0a6f4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6964-40bb-46c9-48a7"}],"description":"## Summary\nThe MCP blue-green autodeploy emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {reason: deploy_failed}` (→ `rebar/host:deploy_errors`, which pages the `rebar-autodeploy-errors` alarm) on TWO conditions that are *documented as routine, non-error backoffs that must be kept OUT of deploy_errors*: `port-exhausted` (retire-cap) and low-memory abort. This false-pages the general \"deploys are failing\" alarm during a normal landing burst, when the deploy is in fact correctly, safely deferring.\n\n## Evidence (live, 2026-08-30 ~03:33–04:05 UTC on i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\nDuring a burst of merges, both blue/green MCP ports (8092/8093) were held by un-reaped containers still in their 21-min graceful drain (`docker stop --time 1260`). Each deploy tick logged BOTH markers for the same event:\n```\nAUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP {reason: port-exhausted, detail: both 8092 and 8093 held by un-reaped mcp containers; not starting a colliding 3rd (cap=3)}\nAUTODEPLOY_ERROR {reason: deploy_failed, detail: component=mcp target=... fail#1..4 backoff=60s..480s}\n```\n`rebar-autodeploy-errors` (deploy_errors, Sum>0 / 4 periods) and `rebar-autodeploy-mcp-retire-cap` BOTH went ALARM. It self-resolved (~04:15 the old container reaped, `b9dd6e3a` cut over, 1 healthy MCP). No outage — MCP served the old build throughout; only the cutover was delayed.\n\n## Root cause\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`:\n- port-exhausted path (~line 780): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP port-exhausted ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n- low-mem path (~line 771): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n- `record_mcp_backoff_failure` (~line 547) calls `err deploy_failed \"component=mcp ...\"` → emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` → inflates `deploy_errors`.\n\nThis contradicts the documented contract in `infra/scripts/observability.sh` (mcp blue-green counters): the retire-cap and mem-abort markers are \"each kept out of AUTODEPLOY_ERROR so a routine retire-cap / memory abort never inflates deploy_errors.\" The SUSTAINED case is already covered by the dedicated `mcp_retire_cap` / `mcp_mem_abort` alarms (\"Sustained = releases not draining / a stuck container\"), so the `deploy_errors` emission on these paths is both wrong and redundant.\n\n## Standing intent — this is a fix, not a behavior decision\nThe intended behavior is documented in observability.sh (routine retire-cap/mem-abort kept out of deploy_errors, dedicated alarms cover the sustained case). The code simply doesn't match it. No ADR / design decision required.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. A routine `port-exhausted` (retire-cap) backoff does NOT emit `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR/deploy_failed` and does NOT increment `deploy_errors`; the `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` marker + `mcp_retire_cap` metric remain the signal.\n2. A routine low-memory abort likewise does NOT inflate `deploy_errors`; `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` + `mcp_mem_abort` remain the signal.\n3. GENUINE MCP deploy failures (build-failed, tag-failed, run-failed, unhealthy) STILL emit `deploy_failed` and page `deploy_errors` (no regression to real-failure alarming).\n4. The mcp backoff throttle (timer/prune) still applies on the routine paths so ticks don't hammer during a drain — only the erroneous deploy_errors emission is removed.\n5. A regression test asserts the observable outcome: the retire-cap/mem-abort paths emit their own marker but NOT `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`, while a real failure emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`.\n\n## Notes\nCheck for duplication against the blue-green target ticket (`panicky-sylphish-foxterrier`) and the MCP graceful-drain-contract bug (`wounded-resident-bushbaby`/b580) before implementing; if already covered, close as duplicate. Fix likely factors the backoff-timer bookkeeping out of the deploy_errors emission in `record_mcp_backoff_failure` (or adds a routine-backoff variant that skips `err deploy_failed`).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","6964-40bb-46c9-48a7"],["relates_to","b580-98b6-d9b7-4817"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","autodeploy","mcp","observability","misleading-signal","ready-to-fix"],"ticket_id":"6ada-6015-8ac3-44f5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy MCP routine backoff (retire-cap port-exhausted / mem-abort) inflates deploy_errors, false-paging the general deploy alarm","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fa8f48bd-0ec8-49f5-bd40-9f4fbf5f7801","4b5dd541-ba86-492c-9aa0-dc9d30bf1995","7d128dcf-627c-4789-81a2-f5afd8a0a6f4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788067386880226001,"uuid":"7b173cea-332e-4c16-aa4e-2b512976d997"}